{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734422",
      "title": "Server-side Routing & Required Configuration",
      "sourceHash": "b15002c4cd3a4ddad74d98b7b1ad0a754d334704056284b1167f2d69f72b94b9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 3.96,
          "en": "So we did now upload our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.96,
          "end": 5.22,
          "en": "and deploy the website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.22,
          "end": 6.78,
          "en": "As a last step, I wanna talk",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.78,
          "end": 10.35,
          "en": "about configuring our project for deployment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.35,
          "end": 14.01,
          "en": "and one important gotcha you should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.01,
          "end": 17.25,
          "en": "You might remember that when we deployed this website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.25,
          "end": 19.98,
          "en": "we were asked whether we wanna configure it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.98,
          "end": 23.583,
          "en": "as a single page application, and we chose yes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.42,
          "end": 26.88,
          "en": "Now this is important, but why?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.88,
          "end": 30.33,
          "en": "Well, keep in mind that on that website we have navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.33,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "We can navigate between different pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 35.22,
          "en": "we can move between these different routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.22,
          "end": 36.93,
          "en": "And what's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.93,
          "end": 40.8,
          "en": "is that this navigation is provided by a React Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.8,
          "end": 44.7,
          "en": "so by a package that's part of our React project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.7,
          "end": 48.15,
          "en": "And that code for evaluating the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.15,
          "end": 51.57,
          "en": "and loading different components executes in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.57,
          "end": 54.03,
          "en": "It's even called react-router-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 55.68,
          "en": "So it's a client side package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.68,
          "end": 57.93,
          "en": "It's not executing on a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.93,
          "end": 59.07,
          "en": "I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.07,
          "end": 62.403,
          "en": "this project has no code that executes on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.24,
          "end": 65.13,
          "en": "Now why is this important?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.13,
          "end": 68.58,
          "en": "Well, it implies that when we click blog here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.58,
          "end": 71.19,
          "en": "the logic for moving to the blog component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.19,
          "end": 74.52,
          "en": "is executed in the browser, not on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.52,
          "end": 76.71000000000001,
          "en": "Now clicking on links is one thing though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.71000000000001,
          "end": 81.71000000000001,
          "en": "What if we enter a URL like the domain /posts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.71000000000001,
          "end": 85.5,
          "en": "then it also loads this blog page as it should,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.5,
          "end": 87.63,
          "en": "but we shouldn't take this for granted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.63,
          "end": 90.53999999999999,
          "en": "Because actually when you have your application deployed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.53999999999999,
          "end": 94.38,
          "en": "on a server and a user enters a URL in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.38,
          "end": 96.24000000000001,
          "en": "what happens technically is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.24000000000001,
          "end": 98.82,
          "en": "the browser sends a request to the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.82,
          "end": 99.99000000000001,
          "en": "That always happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.99000000000001,
          "end": 102.9,
          "en": "because the browser must request the website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.9,
          "end": 105.093,
          "en": "for which we just entered the address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.17,
          "end": 108.45,
          "en": "Now the server then sends back a response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 108.45,
          "end": 111.42,
          "en": "which of course, is in the end is this React application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.42,
          "end": 112.97999999999999,
          "en": "So the HTML file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 112.97999999999999,
          "end": 116.49000000000001,
          "en": "but also the JavaScript code that makes up this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.49000000000001,
          "end": 119.16,
          "en": "Now if we did not just send a request to main domain,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 119.16,
          "end": 122.25,
          "en": "but maybe also to some path like /posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.25,
          "end": 124.86,
          "en": "or whatever path we have on our website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.86,
          "end": 127.35,
          "en": "then that path also reaches the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.35,
          "end": 129,
          "en": "on this initial request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 129,
          "end": 130.83,
          "en": "And by default, the server would try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.83,
          "end": 132.51,
          "en": "to find the fitting response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 132.51,
          "end": 136.02,
          "en": "for the path we requested in our request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 136.02,
          "end": 136.853,
          "en": "For example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.853,
          "end": 139.92000000000002,
          "en": "by searching for a folder with a name of some route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 139.92000000000002,
          "end": 142.74,
          "en": "or posts in our example from before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 142.74,
          "end": 143.573,
          "en": "And of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 143.573,
          "end": 146.79,
          "en": "the server in this case would fail to find a fitting file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 146.79,
          "end": 149.19,
          "en": "because it doesn't have any server side logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 149.19,
          "end": 152.76,
          "en": "for handling requests with different paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 152.76,
          "end": 155.91,
          "en": "What the server should instead do is always return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 155.91,
          "end": 159.9,
          "en": "exactly the same HTML file and the same JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 159.9,
          "end": 162.24,
          "en": "so that this path, which we requested,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 162.24,
          "end": 164.52,
          "en": "can be resolved on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 164.52,
          "end": 167.1,
          "en": "by that JavaScript code we requested,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 167.1,
          "end": 171.12,
          "en": "so by our React app that's using React Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 171.12,
          "end": 174.18,
          "en": "However, as mentioned, the default behavior is not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 174.18,
          "end": 176.82,
          "en": "that the server always returns the same file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 176.82,
          "end": 179.85,
          "en": "Instead by default, it would look for a fitting file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 179.85,
          "end": 182.88,
          "en": "in a fitting folder based on the request we sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 182.88,
          "end": 184.59,
          "en": "And that's why we got this question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 184.59,
          "end": 185.91,
          "en": "whether we want to configure this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 185.91,
          "end": 187.95,
          "en": "as a single page application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 187.95,
          "end": 190.14,
          "en": "By answering this question with yes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 190.14,
          "end": 192.27,
          "en": "Firebase set up some configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 192.27,
          "end": 195.03,
          "en": "which is respected by the Firebase server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 195.03,
          "end": 199.62,
          "en": "which basically tells Firebase to always return index.html",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 199.62,
          "end": 202.623,
          "en": "no matter which kind of path we're requesting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 203.46,
          "end": 206.82,
          "en": "So no matter what comes after our URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 206.82,
          "end": 209.64,
          "en": "Firebase will always return index.html,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 209.64,
          "end": 213.96,
          "en": "which then will always request the same JavaScript files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 213.96,
          "end": 216.6,
          "en": "So this makes sure that client side routing is used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 216.6,
          "end": 218.223,
          "en": "instead of server side routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 219.06,
          "end": 220.53,
          "en": "So here, everything works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 220.53,
          "end": 222.32999999999998,
          "en": "but it is something to be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 222.32999999999998,
          "end": 225.45,
          "en": "because our hosting providers might not ask you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 225.45,
          "end": 227.4,
          "en": "whether you want to configure this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 227.4,
          "end": 229.05,
          "en": "as a single page application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 229.05,
          "end": 230.16,
          "en": "And in such cases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 230.16,
          "end": 233.16,
          "en": "you manually must set up some redirection rule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 233.16,
          "end": 237.32999999999998,
          "en": "that basically forwards all requests to index.html.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 237.32999999999998,
          "end": 239.73,
          "en": "That's why it's important to understand the differences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 239.73,
          "end": 242.4,
          "en": "between client side and service side routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 242.4,
          "end": 244.893,
          "en": "and why we have to configure it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}